## 3. Package restructuring (three reviewer-facing parts)
- New scripts/build_submission_package.py assembles the ZIP mechanically:
    README.md, FINAL_CHECKLIST.md, SHA256SUMS.txt
    01_manuscript/       tex/bib/cls/bst, figures x6, stam-m_ja.pdf (29 p), stam-m_ja_main.pdf (p.1–15),
                         cover_letter_ja.md, README.md
    02_supplementary/    stam-m_ja_supplementary.pdf (p.16–29), tables/ (per_query_results.csv 100 rows,
                         per_query_by_condition.csv, per_query_by_condition_mean5.csv, provenance json), README.md
    03_mdr_scripts_data/ sql_package/ (same file set as build_sql_package.py + GIT_COMMIT), paper/ (frozen
                         sources, SSOT, freeze files, figures), paper_scripts/, verification_logs/, README.md
  Preconditions enforced by the script: PDF newer than TeX, SHA256SUMS_ja.txt matches the working tree,
  verify_all.py --static-only PASS. PDF split uses pypdf (page objects are shared, embedded fonts kept once);
  the supplement start page is detected as the first page whose first text line is "補足資料".
- build_sql_package.py excludes build_submission_package.py (it is not part of sql_package).
- Reviewer-facing READMEs: package/README.md (parts, correspondence table, verification levels 0–3, API-key
  requirement only for level 3, DFT vs synthetic data notice, version history), README_01/02/03, FINAL_CHECKLIST.md
  (English-translation gate: default verify_paper_numbers.py run must exit 0 AND print
  "TeX files audited: 2 (stam-m.tex, stam-m_ja.tex)").

